**Title**: Regressions in v6.6.14 — `pruneToOneRelations` and `getJoinedFilters` crash on field names that aren't direct entity properties

## Summary

Upgrading from v6.6.13 to v6.6.14 causes every `EntityManager.find()` call to throw when the `populate` / `fields` lists contain names that don't correspond to a direct `meta.properties[k]` key — for example star-expanded / computed / aliased paths emitted by an ORM-wrapping layer.

Reproduced consistently against [Medusa v2.14.2](https://medusajs.com)'s `MikroOrmAbstractBaseRepository.find` when `query.graph` resolves field paths like `*employee.company`. Works on 6.6.13; broken on 6.6.14.

## Stack traces

**Trace 1 — `pruneToOneRelations`** (`EntityManager.js:1602`):

```
TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'kind')
  at pruneToOneRelations (EntityManager.js:1602)
  at SqlEntityManager.preparePopulate (EntityManager.js:1623)
  at SqlEntityManager.find (EntityManager.js:128)
  at MikroOrmAbstractBaseRepository_.find
  at AbstractService_.list
  ...
```

**Trace 2 — `getJoinedFilters`** (`EntityManager.js:288`):

```
TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'strategy')
  at SqlEntityManager.getJoinedFilters (EntityManager.js:288)
  at SqlEntityManager.getJoinedFilters (EntityManager.js:298)
  at SqlEntityManager.find (EntityManager.js:146)
  at MikroOrmAbstractBaseRepository_.find
  ...
```

Both originate from the same root cause introduced by PR
[#7664](https://github.com/mikro-orm/mikro-orm/pull/7664)
("merge nested fields paths into explicit populate", commit `f73568a`).

## Root cause

Two `meta.properties[field]` lookups don't guard against `undefined`:

`EntityManager.js:1602` (in `pruneToOneRelations`):

```js
field = field.split(':')[0];
if (!field.includes('.') && ![ReferenceKind.MANY_TO_ONE, ReferenceKind.ONE_TO_ONE]
    .includes(meta.properties[field].kind)) {
  ret.push(field);
  continue;
}
// ...
const prop = meta.properties[key];
if (!prop.targetMeta) { /* ... */ }
```

`EntityManager.js:288` (in `getJoinedFilters`):

```js
for (const hint of options.populate) {
  const field = hint.field.split(':')[0];
  const prop = meta.properties[field];
  const strategy = getLoadingStrategy(
    prop.strategy || hint.strategy || options.strategy || this.config.get('loadStrategy'),
    prop.kind,
  );
```

When `meta.properties[field]` is undefined, the `.kind` / `.targetMeta` / `.strategy` accesses crash.

## Suggested fix

Defensive guards that treat unknown field names as scalars (matching pre-#7664 behaviour):

```diff
 // pruneToOneRelations, line 1602
 field = field.split(':')[0];
-if (!field.includes('.') && ![ReferenceKind.MANY_TO_ONE, ReferenceKind.ONE_TO_ONE].includes(meta.properties[field].kind)) {
+if (!field.includes('.') && (!meta.properties[field] || ![ReferenceKind.MANY_TO_ONE, ReferenceKind.ONE_TO_ONE].includes(meta.properties[field].kind))) {
   ret.push(field);
   continue;
 }
 // ...
 const prop = meta.properties[key];
-if (!prop.targetMeta) {
+if (!prop || !prop.targetMeta) {
   ret.push(key);
   continue;
 }
```

```diff
 // getJoinedFilters, line ~288
 for (const hint of options.populate) {
   const field = hint.field.split(':')[0];
   const prop = meta.properties[field];
+  if (!prop) {
+    continue; // unknown / virtual populate hint — skip JOIN filter computation
+  }
   const strategy = getLoadingStrategy(
     prop.strategy || hint.strategy || options.strategy || this.config.get('loadStrategy'),
     prop.kind,
   );
```

The first hunk is what we shipped as a pnpm patch and verified fixes the first crash end-to-end — until the second crash showed up. The second hunk is the matching guard; we haven't shipped it (we instead pinned back to 6.6.12) but happy to PR it together with a regression test if helpful.

## Impact

Any downstream that wraps mikro-orm and synthesises populate hints beyond direct entity properties is currently blocked from 6.6.14 — i.e. blocked from the GHSA-cfw5-68c4-ffqp / CVE-2026-44680 fix that landed in this release.

Tracking from our side: https://github.com/OneKeyHQ/server-service-b2b/blob/feat/initial-import-from-monorepo/SECURITY.md

### Describe the bug

### Description

Querying with a many-to-many relation filter inside a `$and` clause with 2+ conditions throws an `InvalidFieldNameException: no such column: ...` when using `strategy: 'joined'` and `populateWhere: PopulateHint.INFER` due to incorrect resolution of the pivot table alias in `renameFieldToPK`.

### Example

**Reproduction repo:** https://github.com/chloeelim/mikro-reproduction/tree/joined-strategy-on-many-to-many

```ts
@Entity()
class User {
  @PrimaryKey() id!: number;
  @Property() name: string;
  @ManyToMany(() => Role, 'users', { owner: true }) roles = new Collection<Role>(this);
}

@Entity()
class Role {
  @PrimaryKey() id!: number;
  @Property() title: string;
  @ManyToMany(() => User, 'roles') users = new Collection<User>(this);
}

// throws: `InvalidFieldNameException: no such column: u0.role_id`
await em.findAll(User, {
  where: {
    $and: [
      { roles: { id: { $in: [1] } } },
      { name: { $like: 'User%' } },
    ],
  },
  populate: ['roles'],
  strategy: 'joined',
  populateWhere: PopulateHint.INFER,
});
```

**Note:** This bug seems to have been present since v6.5.0. All three options must be present together to reproduce: populate, strategy: 'joined', and populateWhere: PopulateHint.INFER. Removing any one of them, or reducing $and to a single condition, avoids the error.

