### Describe the bug

In the context of polymorphic relationships:
```TypeScript
defineEntity({
  name: "Owner",
  properties: {
    ...
    poly: () => p.manyToOne([EntityA, EntityB]),
  },
})
```

If one of the target entities has a default filter:
```TypeScript
  name: "EntityA",
  filters: {
    excludeSoftDeleted: {
      name: "excludeSoftDeleted",
      cond: { deletedAt: null },
      default: true,
    },
  },
```

That filter gets applied to select queries for the Owner entity:
```SQL
inner join `entity_a` as `p1`
    on `o0`.`poly_id` = `p1`.`id`
    and `o0`.`poly_type` = 'entity_a'
    and `p1`.`deleted_at` is null
```

Which makes most queries fail, e.g.:
```TypeScript
  const entityB = new EntityB();
  const owner = new Owner();
  owner.poly = entityB;
  orm.em.persist([entityB, owner]);
  await orm.em.flush();

  const forkedEm = orm.em.fork();

  // NotFoundError because EntityA default filter was applied
  // inner join `entity_a` as `p1` on `o0`.`poly_id` = `p1`.`id` and `o0`.`poly_type` = 'entity_a' and `p1`.`deleted_at` is null
  const foundEntity = await forkedEm.findOneOrFail(Owner, {
    id: owner.id,
  });
```

It fails with the PostgreSQL driver, but the repro has been done around SQLite for convenience.

